I see no really good reason why 2.3e wouldn't compile on a bleeding
edge Linux -- the Unix programming interfaces are mostly compatible back
into the 1980s.

But remember that there's a lot of configuration to do *before*
compiling. If you don't get that right you will have the "loads of
compile errors" you describe.

Back in the 2.3e days Linux was probably not the main target, either.
It might be that compiling for (say) Solaris or old SunOS was the
default then, and what required the least manual configuration.

I should give it a try (because it's a good idea!) but don't hold your
breath ...

